{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq7kljz739q","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"Defensibility = context-need GATE (abstain-by-default, minimize regret); no-win on self-solvable tasks is CORRECT","summary":"Reframe after v7 (7th no-win). Product claim is NOT \"context always helps\" — it's \"retrieve context only when it helps, abstain otherwise, so we never pay the over-deliberation tax.\" A no-win on self-solvable specs is then the CORRECT behavior (gate abstains → parity with OFF → zero regret), not a failure. GATE (reuses v7 embeddings): run search_knowledge; confidence = top-1 cosine + margin (sharp specific match vs diffuse topical noise); gate on note TYPE (inject only EMPIRICAL scar-tissue gotchas/decisions/root-causes, never general principles — v4 lesson: topically-relevant-but-general note still hurt); DEFAULT = ABSTAIN. Defensibility ARTIFACT: labeled eval, label = \"OFF underperforms best ON arm\" (ground truth from existing report-v2..v7, no rerun); report REGRET = overhead-when-injected-wrongly + wins-missed-when-abstained-wrongly. On v1–v7 a correct gate ≈0 regret. Headline: \"we measurably do NOT lose where memory doesn't help\" — differentiator vs blind-inject memory products. Ships conservative NOW; INJECT threshold calibrates once the cross-session winning-case experiment yields positive labels. Implemented as task 688a3742.../4.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-10T04:30:12.067Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:01:05.747Z"}
